# NorthernKnife — UGC Scripting

This repo **feeds the Gen 2 system**: the `UGC Creator Library` in Notion and
its `🎬 Creator Script Library`. Scripts written here land as **rows in that
database**. This repo is the drafting and review surface; Notion is where
creators are assigned and work is tracked.

Brand: NorthernKnife (https://northernknife.com/) — hand-forged,
Viking-inspired knives.

Sibling repo: `my-client` (daily TrendTrack → Notion video-brief routine).
Same brand, **different deliverable and a different rulebook**. Do not carry
`my-client`'s format or persona logic over here — see "Where my-client is
wrong for UGC" below.

## Read this first, in order

1. `brand-pack/05-process/ugc-script-process.md` — **authoritative.** The
   unit of work, Script IDs, the five-section page body, every database
   property, b-roll selection, the copy rulebook, pre-flight, delivery, and
   the live breakage to work around.
2. `brand-pack/05-process/observed-notion-structure.md` — field record of how
   the live Notion pages actually look, both generations.
3. `brand-pack/05-process/notion-integration.md` — the collection URLs and
   page IDs to read and write.
4. `brand-pack/01-brand/product-catalog.md` — the only claims you may make.

## The unit of work

**One script = one row** in the Creator Script Library, carrying a long form
and a short form of the *same* script plus three hooks for the edit.

Not a batch. Not two different scripts. Two scripts is the
**per-creator-per-shoot-day limit**. Scaling happens by filling cells in the
format × product matrix (the holiday wave is 6 × 4 = 24 rows), never by
stacking variants inside one page.

## The three guards that get violated

- **Feather — never describe how the pattern got onto the blade.** Not
  etched, not hand-finished, not engraved, **and not laser-applied**. The live
  rule is that it is simply there. The pattern stays the hero of the visuals;
  it just never gets a process word.
- **BJORN Santoku — the word "Japanese" never appears**, nor any nod to
  Japanese origin, tradition or technique, spoken, captioned or styled (no
  kanji packaging, no sushi plating).
- **LOKI Blackout — the bottle opener is in the handle**, not the blade or
  spine.

A creator saying one of these out loud is worse than a brief containing it:
it ships in their voice and can't be fixed in post.

## Where `my-client` is wrong for UGC

`my-client/CLAUDE.md` is the ad-rewriting rulebook. Four of its rules do not
hold here, and following them produces output the live system rejects:

| `my-client` says | UGC reality |
|---|---|
| Feather pattern is **laser-applied**; say so | **Say nothing** about how the pattern got there |
| Persona maps to product (JOHN → Feather/BJORN) | **Avatar follows the format.** Feather runs past MIKE, SARAH and VANCE; JOHN appears in none of the holiday wave |
| Offer lands 60–80% through, never first | True of Gift Testimonial; **`6 I am Mad` puts the offer in the hook** |
| 3 focus products, 4 personas | **7 products and 6 avatars** in the live script schema; 23 knives in the b-roll library |

What *does* carry over: no spec-sheet jargon, plain material plus the
consequence, only real offers, and the mechanic-transfers-but-never-the-words
rule.

## Live scope

- **Script `Product`** (7): LOKI Viking · LOKI Blackout · Feather ·
  BJORN Santoku · RAGNAR Tiger Cleaver · ODIN · Multi / Lineup
- **`Avatar`** (6): SARAH · MIKE · VANCE · JOHN · STEVE · DARIEN
- **`Format`** (12), **`Wave`** (3), **`Markets`** (5) — enumerated in the
  process doc, Section D. Never invent an option the schema doesn't list.
- The b-roll library's `Knives` property carries **23 options** mirroring
  every live knife on the site as of 2026-10-06.

## B-roll

Select from the library; **never mint a shot ID**. Query
`Knives — B-Roll Library` and use what comes back — and check the row is
live, because a fetched page flagged `deleted` is archived and an archived
shot is not a shot.

**As of 2026-10-08 most b-roll references on existing script rows are dead.**
Of the 15 IDs cited by `XM-GT-FTH`, only `KNF-XM12` resolves. Re-resolve any
package before a creator is sent it. Process doc Section I has the detail.

## Where things live

- `brand-pack/05-process/` — the spec, the field notes, the integration map.
- `brand-pack/01-brand/` — product catalog (claim surface) and brand voice.
- `brand-pack/02-personas/` — avatar notes. **Stubs.**
- `brand-pack/03-creator-direction/` — filming rules and b-roll notes.
  The live filming rules live in `briefs/ugc-broll-library/README.md`, which
  is **not in this repo** — see the integration doc.
- `ugc-scripts/<SCRIPT-ID>.md` — markdown mirror of each delivered row, so
  scripts are reviewable in git and survive a Notion edit. Start from
  `_template.md`.

## Delivery

A script is delivered when it exists as a row in the Creator Script Library
with every property set and a resolving b-roll package — then mirrored to
`ugc-scripts/` and committed. **A script that exists only in this repo has not
been delivered.** If the Notion connector isn't available in a run, say so
explicitly rather than silently skipping delivery.

## Scaffold status

The process spec, the integration map and the product guards are current as of
2026-10-08 and were read from the live workspace. The **persona/avatar docs and
brand-voice doc are still stubs** marked `TODO(brand-pack)` — including STEVE
and DARIEN, for whom nothing is known beyond the name. Do not invent brand
facts to fill them.
